# Line endings are decided here rather than by whatever core.autocrlf each machine happens
# to be set to. Without this, a file written with LF and one written with CRLF both end up
# in the index as LF, and git narrates every one of them:
#
#   warning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in <file>
#
# which is noise on every single commit, and hides any warning worth reading.
#
# text=auto keeps the repository on LF — the right thing for a repo that CI and non-Windows
# machines also build — while leaving each working tree to check out whatever suits it. No
# existing file changes: the index is already LF.
* text=auto

# Binary files are never converted. A line ending "fixed" inside a PDF or a .boc is a
# corrupted file, and the corruption is silent.
*.pdf binary
*.db  binary
*.boc binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
